---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
const plans = site.pricing.plans;
---
<Legal
  title="Terms and conditions"
  description={`The terms on which ${site.name} sells memberships and runs classes.`}
>
  <p>
    These are the terms between you and {site.legal.entityName} when you buy a membership or attend a
    class at our studios in Anjar and Adipur. Buying a membership means you accept them.
  </p>

  <h2>What we sell</h2>
  <p>
    In-person yoga classes at our two studios. A membership is a pass for a period of time, not a
    fixed number of classes. Current plans and prices:
  </p>
  <ul>
    {plans.map((p) => <li>{p.name}, ₹{p.price.toLocaleString('en-IN')}</li>)}
  </ul>
  <p>
    Prices are in Indian rupees and include any taxes that apply. We may change prices at any time,
    but never for a membership you have already paid for.
  </p>

  <h2>How a membership works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>One membership works at both studios. Come to whichever suits you that day.</li>
    <li>
      It runs by date, from the day it starts to the day it ends. Classes you miss are not carried
      over and do not extend it.
    </li>
    <li>It belongs to you and cannot be shared with or transferred to anyone else.</li>
    <li>Your first class is free, so you can try before you pay for anything.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your health</h2>
  <p>
    Yoga is physical exercise. We are yoga teachers, not doctors, and nothing we say is medical
    advice or treatment.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Tell the teacher before class about any injury, illness, surgery, pregnancy, or medicine that
      affects what you can do. We will adapt the class for you.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you have a heart condition, high or low blood pressure, a recent injury or operation, or you
      are pregnant, please speak to your doctor before starting.
    </li>
    <li>
      Work at your own pace. Stop if something hurts. Never push into pain because the person next to
      you is going further.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You take part at your own risk. As far as the law allows, we are not responsible for injury,
    illness, or loss of belongings at the studio, except where it is caused by our own negligence.
    Please do not leave valuables in the changing area.
  </p>

  <h2>In the studio</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Arrive a few minutes early. Latecomers may be asked to wait for a suitable moment to join.</li>
    <li>Phones on silent, please.</li>
    <li>
      We may ask someone to leave, without a refund, if their behaviour makes the class unsafe or
      unpleasant for others.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Timetable changes and closures</h2>
  <p>
    Timings can change and studios close on some public holidays. We will tell members on WhatsApp
    where we reasonably can. If we have to cancel classes for a long period, talk to us and we will
    put it right.
  </p>

  <h2>Payments</h2>
  <p>
    You can pay in cash at the studio, by UPI, or online through Razorpay when that is switched on.
    A membership starts once the payment reaches us. If a payment fails or is reversed, the
    membership does not start.
  </p>

  <h2>Refunds</h2>
  <p>
    Set out on the <a href="/refunds/">refunds and cancellation page</a>, which forms part of these
    terms.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    We try to keep the timetable and prices on this site correct, but mistakes happen. If a price
    here is obviously wrong, we are not obliged to honour it. Photographs and text on this site
    belong to us; please do not copy them.
  </p>

  <h2>Law</h2>
  <p>
    These terms are governed by the law of India. Any dispute will be dealt with by the courts of
    Kutch, Gujarat.
  </p>
</Legal>
